29,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Rin,,The bin house at the station block smells really bad in summer! And the supervised mornings take almost an hour.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Midori,,"A shelter is expensive, even with a subsidy. Also, we're already spending over thirty thousand yen a year on basic maintenance.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Most complaints come from the person whose gate it's by. Also, nobody actually wants to be the ""bin police"" and turn bags away.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,May,,"The truck comes very early, and those supervised mornings are a real time commitment. It's not just a quick check.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"Not all our frontages are the same size; some are too narrow. Plus, the ward requires a lot of paperwork for permanent builds.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Midori, is thirty thousand yen a lot? I don't want it to be smelly or expensive!","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Midori,,"It adds up, Rin. @Asuka, if the paperwork is hard, maybe a permanent structure isn't the best way to keep peace.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Exactly. If we force people to police each other, we'll just have more arguments.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you're right. If the truck arrives before some people wake up, a strict window is just stressful.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@May, then rotating the location might be the only fair way, provided the space allows it.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But if we move it, does that mean it'll be by my house too?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Midori,,"It would be fair, but we have to check if everyone's front is wide enough.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, did the measurements show that it's even possible to move it to every house?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,May,,I just don't want one person doing all the work. Rotating the spot at least rotates the burden.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"One house is too narrow and another has a driveway. It wouldn't be perfectly equal, but it's better than one person suffering.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I don't like the smell of the bin house, so let's not build one!","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree. The cost and the maintenance of a structure seem too risky for our budgets.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"If we avoid the ""police"" role and the expensive build, we're left with moving it.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,May,,Rotating seems the least exhausting in the long run.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Asuka,,It's the most logical choice given the constraints.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
